is mechanism may very well actually be the goal of the God Machine in relation for humanity in the first place. Stop angels from Falling not by fixing the bug which allows them to fall (that's impossible because entropy) but by making the environment they hide among so hostile that it would become very easy to root them out. A different solution to the same problem. And by doing so, the God Machine will be able to fulfill the ancient promise it made for humanity ages ago, that they, too, could become like God. That they, too, could return to Eden.<br /> <br /> That what rise must fall- but what's fallen may rise again.<br /> <br /> Let's just hope that God won't become sick beforehand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you mention Frailty. I once saw on an OLD thread that the idea with KoSA was &quot;Roadhouse meets Frailty&quot; which gave me a VERY clear vision on how to play on the more disturbing and gritty aspects of the conspiracy (instead of simply being stupid cool bounty hunters).<br /> <br /> Also, here's a possibility for why it took so long for America. The conspiracy is Infrastructure itself. Possible Defense Infrastructure, but that's not the point. The point being that an occult matrix us need for the angel to be able to bestow Ink. I don't know what the soldiers of Jabreel differered on thematically, but it could be assumed they had everything they needed for the angel to get to work.<br /> <br /> But America didn't at the time. Until skip tracing and bounty hunting (and likely more). Once that came into play, America was all set for the angel, and the Knights of St Adrian were born","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T15:45:50-08:00","id":1474527,"title":"","content":"The KoSA here (with mentions of skiptracing) reminds me of a dated Korean tv drama (a \u2018fictional historical\u2019) \u201cThe Slave Chasers,\u201d named after and motifs taken from slave-returners (people who capture back fugitive slaves\u2026 or innocents illegally framed so) who operated in middle to late Joseon dynasty. That same name could\u2019ve been a Cover for the Knights/Soldiers in that age and area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T16:17:14-08:00","id":1474532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1473595-conspiracy-theory-the-supplementary?p=1474511#post1474511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the interesting thing is that the KoSA are an American organization, yet the USA is known to not be very Catholic- but still, I am not going to claim to understand American Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The writeup doesn't specify a region of the US, but the amount of space in the American West makes it easy to associate with both long-haul trucking and people finding places to disappear to while running from debts and bounties; the American West is also the part of the country closer to its southern border with a country with a long history of (variously syncretized) Catholicism.<br /> <br /> Back east, Irish and Italian Americans have a fairly lengthy history of cultural Catholicism \u2014 it's part of the package of conflict those groups had with their neighbors when their families immigrated to the States.<br /> <br /> Most American Presidents haven't been Catholic, and there was that whole business with the Puritans at the start and whatnot, but\u2026 <a href=\"https://bigthink.com/culture-religion/dominant-religions-in-the-us-county-by-county/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;not Catholic&quot; isn't really the American religious identity circa the 1990s, especially in places densely-populated enough for God to get a machine running that can exploit debt-collection services</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if we are to take all of those factors together, we can start to get a glimpse of what is actually going on with the KoSA- a certain organization revolving a certain archangel with the power to gift humans with divine gifts through stigmata. That angel seems to have formed numerous conspiracies throughout the years- how many we don't know, but wherever there is religion and there is God there are His Hounds seeking out demons. Those hunters, as it seems, serve as a &quot;bridge&quot; between humanity and God- which could explain why the angel didn't Fell through the years. </div> </div> </div>A couple things to remember:<br /> <br /> 1. The Demon part of Empire of Gold and Dust shows us the angel backing the Soldiers of Jabreel, who is Rank 2 (and therefore, in the logic of angelic Rank, not a significantly major part of the Machine's plans) and acts as patron of &quot;the current incarnation of&quot; the Soldiers. Ink and its predecessors are probably not unique tech, given this.<br /> <br /> 2. Empire of Gold and Dust also introduces a lot of variant mechanics for pacts \u2014 including one germane to the offer Casey Howard got a week before she met the angel \u2014 and it's kind of a major part of Demon's themes and mood that there's nothing strictly preventing the client from being a demon themself. Even if the Knights and the Soldiers <i>do</i> have the same patron, that doesn't mean that patron didn't Fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-12-2022, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T16:55:24-08:00","id":1474535,"title":"","content":"It seems I have missed Amal's section in the Era- for in my defense, the fact we have an angel with some very hilarious name after him took most of my attention. Amal is indeed not likely to be the same patron as the modern Knights (they are very clearly being contracted by an angel, IMO- you could say that he is secretly a demon, but it would subvert, well, everything about the Knights' themes so I would not suggest it. Could work, sure, but not something I would go for). In that case, I would either go with the different angels which work the Knights-by-any-other-name as part of the same Infrastructure, which by itself would be a archangel which keeps the conspiracy going, and wherever the Infrastructure pf that archangel spreads it can grant the boons now known as Ink. Amal, in that case, would be more like a Royal Avatar or other lower manifestation of the archangel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T19:19:09-08:00","id":1474542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1473595-conspiracy-theory-the-supplementary?p=1474535#post1474535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, I would either go with the different angels which work the Knights-by-any-other-name as part of the same Infrastructure, which by itself would be a archangel which keeps the conspiracy going, and wherever the Infrastructure pf that archangel spreads it can grant the boons now known as Ink. Amal, in that case, would be more like a Royal Avatar or other lower manifestation of the archangel.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the interest of keeping terminology clear, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/74456-detecting-god-machine-infrastructure-with-awakened-magic?p=75888#post75888\">a reminder about what Infrastructure is</a>. Infrastructure is a particular subset of ways the world is weird, in this case by being things the Machine can arrange to generate outputs. The descriptions of both Ink and the Soldiers' finely-wrought jewelry would seem to indicate that the tats are just magical items/substances generated at a secondary location and transported with the client \u2014 the ability to bestow the Endowment isn't a mechanical element on Amal's character sheet any more than their ability to hand you four-hundred dollars they had in their pocket would be.<br /> <br /> Available evidence suggests that angels don't do autonomous sub-manifestations like Royal Avatars. If an angel needs to be in multiple places at once, it's built to do that or it's equipped with tools or dispatched to areas that allow it to do that, but there's no need to let an angel section off a piece of the free will it's not supposed to have to do a smaller job when doing smaller jobs is the point of angels in the first place. It could be that there's a higher-Ranking Wheel whose Mission includes seeing to it that whatever unit is managing the Specially-Equipped Anti-Demon Task Force this century stays on-message while it coordinates Eyes at the drop points and keeps Swords on intersecting assignments from running into the Knights, but that's a prosaic superior in a systemic hierarchy rather than a greater ego from which Amal and their peers are derived.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Machine uses mundane components whenever possible unless it thinks it would be more efficient/have a greater margin of success to use a supernatural element. The Knights don't need to be part of an occult matrix serving an extension of an archangel to be a hit-squad directed by a Messenger with access to counter-demonic magical equipment; if running riot on a bunch of Integrators or subverting a Temporal Agency could accomplish the same results with less trouble, the Machine would go for that instead, but for the moment the Knights are its preferred approach to this problem in that part of time and space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T03:36:39-08:00","id":1474557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1473595-conspiracy-theory-the-supplementary?p=1474542#post1474542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the interest of keeping terminology clear, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/74456-detecting-god-machine-infrastructure-with-awakened-magic?p=75888#post75888\">a reminder about what Infrastructure is</a>. Infrastructure is a particular subset of ways the world is weird, in this case by being things the Machine can arrange to generate outputs. The descriptions of both Ink and the Soldiers' finely-wrought jewelry would seem to indicate that the tats are just magical items/substances generated at a secondary location and transported with the client \u2014 the ability to bestow the Endowment isn't a mechanical element on Amal's character sheet any more than their ability to hand you four-hundred dollars they had in their pocket would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems I wasn't very clear about that part- the idea was that in order to produce/bestow the Endowment, you need an Infrastructure to which the angel is connected/from which it is produced. Even if the Amal does not directly grant Ink, its ability to do so is granted by the Infrastructure, which in turn is governed by a archangel, and the theory in here is that Amal was summoned using the same Infrastructure which produces the Endowment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Available evidence suggests that angels don't do autonomous sub-manifestations like Royal Avatars. If an angel needs to be in multiple places at once, it's built to do that or it's equipped with tools or dispatched to areas that allow it to do that, but there's no need to let an angel section off a piece of the free will it's not supposed to have to do a smaller job when doing smaller jobs is the point of angels in the first place. It could be that there's a higher-Ranking Wheel whose Mission includes seeing to it that whatever unit is managing the Specially-Equipped Anti-Demon Task Force this century stays on-message while it coordinates Eyes at the drop points and keeps Swords on intersecting assignments from running into the Knights, but that's a prosaic superior in a systemic hierarchy rather than a greater ego from which Amal and their peers are derived. </div> </div> </div>Noted, but on the other hand vast entities of demigod like power have instances of producing sub entities as part of themselves. We don't know if archangels can produce sub angels, but we shouldn't be surprised if it is possible. Again, it could just be that Amal is a product of a wider Infrastructure which in turn is related to an archangel, and then as far as I am concerned it is all about semantics- it doesn't matter, as far as the theory is concerned, whether Amal and Knights' client are the same entity, subsouls of it, products of the same Infrastructure governed by an archangel or being related through any other methodology. The key part of this theory is that all angels which contract the different incarnations of the conspiracy which, in turn, is related to an Infrastructure which its establishment and reach define the God Machine's ability to bestow stigmata, and that there is a high Ranked angel (probably an archangel) which has the mission of &quot;make humans more 'angelic'&quot;. The exact details of how those angels relate to one another and to the Infrastructure are less important, but that is the key behind the theory<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, the Machine uses mundane components whenever possible unless it thinks it would be more efficient/have a greater margin of success to use a supernatural element. The Knights don't need to be part of an occult matrix serving an extension of an archangel to be a hit-squad directed by a Messenger with access to counter-demonic magical equipment; if running riot on a bunch of Integrators or subverting a Temporal Agency could accomplish the same results with less trouble, the Machine would go for that instead, but for the moment the Knights are its preferred approach to this problem in that part of time and space. </div> </div> </div>Sure, the Knights don't need to be a part of something larger than a temporal creation when and where the God Machine finds a need and when the conditions are right- but defining the said conditions is important, IMO, because asking those questions is one of the things I'm doing in this thread :P And sure, they don't need to be anything more than a hit squad, but again, this is a conspiracy theory- the premise in here is &quot;things are not as simple as they seems&quot;, or else the LM would have been left as a bunch of manipulated shamans, for example. Complicating things needlessly is part of the things I enjoy doing here in this thread, after all. Now, generally I think how the conspiracy has plans towards the supernatural, but in some cases (like the LM, the CoB and the KoSA) the relations are so unbalanced that it is hard to envision a state where the hunters have a plan set in motion and manipulate the supernatural. The KoSA especially, as they really gain everything from the God Machine and have little understand or care about its true nature. In that case, the KoSA would probably be fine with whatever plans God has for them (as long as, you know, it won't get them killed), so I presented a scenario where the God Machine have greater plans to the KoSA and all of their previous forms than &quot;god and kill demons for me&quot;. Is it the most logical scenario? No, but I am working with limited lore and seek to complicate things needlessly so this is what we got :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T05:50:17-08:00","id":1474728,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Merrick Institute</b></span><br /> <br /> Because if we can get a Hunter supplement as a Beast stretch goal why not?<br /> <br /> The Merrick Institute is found in an interesting position within the world of Hunter- it is not about being decentralized, of course, and even not about them being mostly teens and young adults. It is that this conspiracy is in fact, <i>not</i> the conspiracy. It is not even a chapter of it, or even its remnants for a future organization. What we have here is a far weirder situation- a cuspule in time, the transition between organizations which involves a bloody civil war, and that while we get something which serves as a playable splat, the actual, true conspiracy is found behind the scenes- the Nameless Organization (as they are going to be referred in here), the dark entity which have formed the children, and which replaces its own form on a regular basis in order to not get caught by either the monsters, other hunters, and of course- their own former slaves.<br /> <br /> Let's dwell on it for a bit.<br /> <br /> In the context of the wider CofD, it is very easy to see the resemblance between Merrick and Deviants- in both cases we have people who got abused by the larger conspiracy which is found within a complex network of false aliases and facilities. It is clear that whatever the true identity of the Nameless Organization may be, they are, with no doubt, part of the Web of Pain. Now, Merrick share that resemblance with VASCU, something which their writeup even mentions, but where VASCU had Dr. Wintergreen to supervise the experiments which somehow brought less.. painful results, the powers behind the Nameless are far less kind- which should tell you something about them. The fact that the Nameless have turned to experiment <i>on children</i> is horrifying all on its own, especially when you consider that they don't really know the criteria required in order to produce a dreamwalker- they just seek after candidates among teens, get most of them killed and then those who survive ends up enslaved for further researched. Overall, they are true evil incarnated, no doubt about it.<br /> <br /> But they are also Vigilante.<br /> <br /> Here is the thing- the Vigil exists in order to blur the lines- it doesn't matter how or why you uphold it as long as in the end, you fight the darkness. And that is something that the Nameless actually does- they experiment on children in order to make them into weapons against the Beasts and other nightmarish horrors which lurk in the collective soul of humanity. In the end, even with all of their horrifying acts, the Nameless do fight monsters through their many incarnations and guises- <i>but that doesn't make them the good guys</i>. They are evil to their core, and they are definitely part of the Web of Pain in terms their actions have probably produced a fair share of Deviants, but through that research they have actually managed to produce a stable system which would grant Endowments to the survivors of their experiments. Who knows? Perhaps if the children were to be maintained under control, the Nameless could have found a way to stabilize the process, to gain more information about the criteria, to minimize the damage caused to the subjects. Maybe if they were to keep their research, they would eventually have produced improved method, eventually becoming a conspiracy with dirty secrets in its closet, but one which does not longer requires abuse in order to fight the monsters. VASCU, after all, have been through the same process, and Lady Lucifuge still uses unsavory methods in order to imprint her Will upon her agents. All conspiracies have elements of abuse within them, and many have probably started in a similar fashion for the Nameless- performing horrible experiments on people in order to develop new tools to fight the darkness. All conspiracies were born in the Web of Pain- we are just not aware of their dirty past, and once the conspiracy is too big to fail, it doesn't matter what kinds of horrible acts they have done as long as they maintain the Vigil, in their own way.<br /> <br /> An interesting insight indeed- but totally irrelevant. The Nameless were fallen, and now we have the Merrick Institute, right?<br /> <br /> Well... it's complicated. We are going to return for it later.<br /> <br /> Beforehand, what we want to examine is the exact details of the Merrick process. Now, we know that we don't know much about the process for the simple fact that even the Nameless weren't really aware for the needed requirements- after all, if they did, they would have been much more efficient in their production of &quot;dream warriors&quot;. What we do know that it requires the use of teens, and that through chemical and other traumatic methods, they can force those children into projecting into the Astral, allowing them to fight Beasts in their Lairs. We also know that they require some kind of an aptitude for the process to work, or else the process would have been much more successful (aka, less dead children). That makes sense, considering how most things which are connected to the Primordial Dream require a certain aptitude to form a connection- souls which resonate with the darker aspects of the Dream draw the attention of the Dark Mother and ends up Devoured, while those with a sensitive connection to the ripples caused by primordial hunger ends up as Oracles and Heroes, meant to both to warn and fight those horrors. The second type of souls seems to resonate the most with the children of Merrick- but if that's so, if those children have a natural connection to the Dream and have a natural affinity to fight it, why do the Nameless work so hard in order to produce those horrifying effects? Is it simply about their need to control? Or maybe it is because they just don't understand what they are doing? Or maybe it is something else- maybe the process is abusive because there is a reason for that abuse. After all, most children ends up scarred physically and mentally by the horrifying process...<br /> <br /> What is what the Nameless do isn't abuse- what if it is a Devouring?<br /> <br /> I mean, it would make some sense- the Merrick process is in fact a artificial Devouring, produced by the Nameless in order to awaken the hidden potential of future Heroes (heck, maybe even future Beasts) in order to chain them up and use their talents for the benefit of the Vigil. In the eyes of the Nameless it may even be <i>moral-</i> remember the Code. Monsters don't count. Monsters are the enemy. Sure, you can work with a monster, you can even protect a monster, but doing so is a compromise- and once you prioritize monstrous life over human life, you violate the Code. If hunters have their mentality modified by the Vigil, and the children of Merrick (like most other conspiracy hunters) are indeed monsters-to-be, then the hunters of the Nameless won't even view what they are doing as a abuse. After all, what they are doing is to save people from becoming monsters, and using their abilities to fight the darkness. Sure, innocents may get killed in the process- but those were all suspected or future monsters. It is a sacrifice which has to be made if they wish to protect the world. Don't get me wrong- what the Nameless are doing is disgusting and horrible, but we have other groups who do disgusting and horrible things and get out of it only because they are doing it to monsters. The Abbey, Cheiron, the Faithful, the Promethean Brotherhood- all of those groups and more are made of horrible people who manage to get out of it because their horrible actions are done towards monsters. If, in the eyes of the Nameless, the children of Merrick are potential monsters, and would become monsters unless they'll go through the Merrick process, then aren't they, technically, already monsters? And if they are already monsters, then using their horrifying methods on them doesn't count as harming the innocents, because they <i>are not people</i>. And if that's true, then by forcing their own version of a Devouring, one which maims and controls the destructive urges of those monsters, they not only stop a potential monster from causing harm, they actually stop the monster from being made- and wouldn't that, indeed, fall under the definition of the Vigil?<br /> <br /> Maybe- but it still doesn't make the Nameless into the good guys. They suck- but they are still hunters.<br /> <br /> And worse- they are still around.<br /> <br /> We get it in their writeup, after all- Merrick was dismantled, but the Nameless are still around. True to a part of the Web of Pain, the Nameless still have their own facilities working around the US (and maybe beyond it), doing horrible things while keeping their research going on. Here and there, Merrick find those facilities and fight them, liberating the trapped children- but considering their tendency to replace their own names and faces, it is very clear that the Nameless, in whatever form they may take, are still around, and they probably want to take over their rogue faction. Again, we should take into perspective that in their eyes, the Merrick children are monsters- tamed monsters but still monsters. When they kill, kidnap and brainwash those children, they, in their mind, fight monsters. On the other hand, the hunters of Merrick view they tormentors as monsters- and as such do what they can in order to stop the Nameless and dismantle it once and for all. That cycle of abuse is a product of the Code getting twisted, of hunters targeting each other as monsters and justifying the means through it. That is a dark and unpleasant corner of the Vigil- one which we can finally examine through the eyes of Merrick, and a cautionary tale which could happen for any conspiracy if they are not careful enough.<br /> <br /> When we take all of it into account, we can get one thing very, very clearly- that Merrick are not the true conspiracy, they are its sins and past taking form, working to punish a rouge conspiracy for falling too deep into the darkness in their quest to fight it. Merrick <i>could</i> become it, sure, but in their current state they are \\far too decentralized to do so. Heck, they are currently during their own civil war (one without bloodshed, however... for now) over whether or not they <i>should</i> become a conspiracy. Because let's be honest, if the Firebrand would win, there will be no Merrick- there will be no further research, no new attempts for recruitment, no steady access for resources meant to maintain a organization. They don't even have a supernatural patron working to unify them like other decentralized conspiracies has. At best scenario, they would defeat the Nameless once and for all and get disbanded afterwards. At the most likely scenario, they would disintegrate into small cells and vanish from the world while the Nameless still lurk in the Web of Pain. At the worst case scenario, the Nameless would take over the small cells one by one, devouring them back into their own organization. There is no &quot;lasting legacy&quot; situation for the Firebrands. The Reformers, on the other hand, are the ones who try to rebuild the conspiracy from the remnants, researching the Merrick process and seek to keep the conspiracy going, yet without the dark methods of the Nameless. If they'll success at the process, then they are very likely to manage to replace the Nameless, caring their candle while leading for a brighter future... but if the process does indeed requires abuse to work, if it is indeed a artificial Devouring, would the Reformers try to minimize the damage but would still perform the experiments? Will they be willing to make the needed sacrifices in order to keep the Vigil going? Will they pay the price- and if so, will they be any different from the Nameless which they have displaced?<br /> <br /> Those questions become even more clear when we examine the potential endgames for the Nameless and Merrick- at first, we thought that each of those probably have their own endgame, but after doing the research I am not so sure. It seems that both organizations want, more or less, the same thing- a world without abuse. A world without nightmares. A world where people can sleep soundly at night, that there is no fear from the dark. The thing is that the Nameless have a much more clear vision about their ideal world- a existence where the darkness is being chained, that the nightmares are bound, that the hungry get devoured. That control over the primordial hunger and chaining it is the key to save the world from it. All of that makes me think about that section in After the Fall, where it mentions how nightmares were bound in Constantinople before the invasion and now they got freed- maybe the Nameless are as old as the Byzantine Empire? Who knows. Merrick, on the other hand, are yet to have a coherent vision- end abuse by destroying the Nameless, sure, and fight other nightmarish abusers, no problem, but what they want to do with it? What to do next? Are they going to take the fight against the Web of Pain, attacking its Astral manifestation in order to force people to face their own fears? Or will they take the fight directly against the embodiment of fear, potentially slaying the Dark Mother herself? The fact that the Reformers have opened a lab in Australia in order to have a better understanding of the Primordial Dream from the aboriginals means that, again, this who method may be ancient- and maybe the old Australian version of the conspiracy could offer the solution for a world without abuse while still changing future heroes or Beasts into dreamwalkers- or perhaps offer their own variation of the Endowment. The Nameless, on the other end, could turn into even darker path- that if the children can't be controlled, they need harsher leashes. Like, potentially, binding their sleeping minds into jaded agents which know what they are doing, and will not fight against the conspiracy even if they'll discover the true dirty secrets that the conspiracy hides...<br /> <br /> Welcome to Merrick. The Vigil has never been darker.<br /> <br /> (next- the last conspiracy: the Hototogisu! What will happen from there? let's wait and see)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 02-25-2022, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T20:08:13-08:00","id":1474778,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s quite the interesting take I\u2019d have to say, Artificial Devouring was unexpected yet fits really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T13:16:37-08:00","id":1475463,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Hototogisu</b></span><br /> <br /> Finally, it is time for the Cuckoo.<br /> <br /> As being part of Tokyo's setting, the Hototogisu was part of the so called &quot;metaplot experiment&quot;- creating a localized, updating, evolving setting which adds more lore and introduce changes as new core books are getting released. Personally, I was quit a fan of the concept, and the Hototogisu were clearly at the center of it all- a strange organization of mortals which have managed to take control over the local vampire population through extorsion, and then started working its way through the all different supernatural societies of the CofD. Led by a merchant known as Inoue Akio, the Hototogisu have grown to become a powerhouse in Tokyo's shadows, even growing beyond Japan as they research the supernatural to develop new products to trade. While some people may be quick to disregard hunters as a threat for the main protagonists of other gamelines, the Hototogisu stands as an example to show that mortals can not just challenge their rule- <i>but they can actually win</i>. At the latest point in the setting, the Hototogisu have more or less formed contacts with every supernatural society, becoming a power to consider. Heck, the organization's power have grown so much, that Inoue have became Tokyo's <i>apex</i>- the strongest, scariest, most influencing horror among horrors, that leaves its mark on the Primordial Dream. His shadow strikes fear all across Tokyo, making him what other monsters fear- a plain old mortal.<br /> <br /> Or is he?<br /> <br /> Here is the thing- even the text doesn't seem to know what Inoue actually is. He was claimed a mortal in the original writeup. He was then claimed to be a ghoul in Beast. Heck, in the same breath, Beast also mentions Inoue as ancient vampire (like, sure, the book doesn't say that the vampire Inoue and the ghoul Inoue are the same Inoue- but considering the connection of both characters to vampires... well, it's fishy saying the least). And that without considering that while the conspiracy was founded after WW2, there was another Hototogisu which, again, was founded by a mortal merchant named Inoue Akio. I mean, sure, that Inoue may be one of the other tow Inoues, considering that vampires and ghouls do tend to live long but... come on, that's just weird. As it seems, we could very well have at least three Inoue Akio, which are always merchants and always have connection to the darkness, vampires especially. Seriously- what the heck? We can't even tell how many Inoue Akios we have in the setting, not to mention how many Hototogisus we also got. Something is fishy in here, sure- and it grows even more fishy once we consider that Lair Trait that Inoue projects into the Hive- Maze. Inoue forms strange patterns and process which makes those who try to follow the Hive to get lost unless they manage to understand which is the right way, solve the riddle, unlocking the cipher.<br /> <br /> Sounds very demonic, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Now, I am not suggesting that Inoue is a demon- on the surface it would make sense. Resurfaced identity and strange patterns is something which resonates well with Demon, and even the Endowments of the organization, Setto, have some demonic quality to them- elements of trade and taking parts of a monster's identity, denying them from it in the process. However, while it makes sense on the surface, things become weird when you start to examine the pieces- first, Inoue seems very much like the opposite of a Cover. It is the same identity shared by multiple individuals, instead of a degrading identity meant to hide from the angels of the God Machine. That makes me think much more on Yodogiri from Durarara, which strangely, also has some connection to vampires. Really, I wonder if the novels were part of a inspiration for the conspiracy. Still, the other thing we need to take into account is Setto- while the modern conspiracy seems to use certain charms as ways to fight the supernatural, they may very well just be an evolution of the general concept offered by the Edo version of the conspiracy (and from what I heard, in a Tokyo game ran by the original writer the Hototogisu hunters did had Setto so... yeah it is still relevant). At any case, while Setto looks like a demonic pact of some kind, what we need to remember that it is a subversion of it- in Demons, pacts are, more or less, a &quot;fair game&quot;. Sure, demons can and do manipulate mortals into giving them those parts they want and keep loopholes in the contracts to keep it in their benefit for a time of need, but it is still, at its essence, a fair trade- the demon gives what they agreed to give in exchange for the mortals giving what they agreed to give. Setto is something different- it is literally means &quot;theft&quot;. Through Setto, the hunter actually steals parts of their target's power, giving nothing in return- that violates the very basic premise of a pact, which means that even if it uses the same mechanism as Cover and Soul Pacts, it is much more insidious in nature. Add to this the fact that in Hunter's terms, Immortality is also a Dread Power- and you could easily see that, in theory, Inoue could indeed be the vampire, the ghoul and the mortal all at the same time. The same crafty merchant which stole <i>a vampire's immortality</i>, confusing the heck out of anyone who tries to get what he actually is. Again, returning back to the &quot;Sins of the Vigilant&quot; meta-conspiracy theory, as users of monstrous power the Hototogisu seems to represent Deception, which is not a cardinal sin per see but it does have a 1e Maeljin associated with it, which is enough for me.<br /> <br /> Ok, so lies and deception seems to be the theme for the Cuckoo- but <i>why the Cuckoo</i>?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm not sure- in classical Japanese culture, the Hototogisu seems to be related to death (spitting blood and crying) while also being a symbol for beauty thanks for its singing, which doesn't really resonate with the organization. On the other hand, a infernal bird does make you think of a certain winged entity which is known to torment vampires- the Strix, and that would once again enforce a connection to vampires is general- but we also need to remember that Tokyo is known to have actual Strix in the form of the Tengu. Does it change anything? Not necessary, but something to keep in mind. At any case, the name itself seems to be much more related to the western concepts of the Cuckoo- a bird known for deception, lies, mimicry and theft, all things which makes work for the conspiracy... but again, those are Western concepts, and here we are talking about the Edo period which is before a rapid exchange of ideas and influence from the West. Still, I am no expert on Japanese culture so, like, it could be that those concepts about a liar cuckoo were already around during Edo and my great Google research simply didn't found it. As I have no Japanese friends to ask about it and I know the writer lived in Japan, I am just going to accept that it could potentially make sense- the Hototogisu are beautiful liars, related to the blood spitting dead and steal what they want from them through cunning and manipulation. Yes, all makes sense- but before we call it a day, let's add another part to the equation. Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Or more specifically- Sundered World.<br /> <br /> One of the main things we got from Sundered World was the existence of the Pangaeans- great beast gods of tremendous power, serving as pillars of reality. Those entities do not just serve as totems of their species but also as symbols of wider meanings- Wolf was, for example, the God of the Hunt. Bull was Kingship and Civilization. Bird was Cruelty. Snake was Poison and Medicine. Those entities were tremendous powers which have either died or changed after the fall of Pangaea, but they have left their mark upon the world, and their influence was not limited to Pangaea, Shadow and the Flesh- through their sheer resonance alone, those demigods were also connected with the Supernal (they were just <i>that real</i> compared to the rest of the world), and many had connections to other worlds as well. Death Wolf and Snake have relations to the Underworld, Bird have created her own pocket dimension, Fox seems to have some ties to the Hedge, Spring may have found a place in the Astral... heck even the Eater of Names may have some very suspicious connections to Duat. It is little wonder that a lot of people even considered Owl to be a Pangaean from which the Strix were created- but maybe it wasn't the case. Maybe we have another bird which was lurking in the shadows, resonating with the themes of Deception and lies which fit the Kindred so well, parasites that play at being humans, stealing their life while spitting blood. Could it be that the Hototogisu are in fact controlled by a Pangaean?<br /> <br /> Unlikely- but it still may have presence in there.<br /> <br /> I mean, if Cuckoo the Pangaean is connected to the Hototogisu it could explain the universal thematic of lies and deception it carries. Pangaeans don't care about culture, after all- they are symbols, and the Cuckoo is a symbol of lies and falsehoods. As such, it would make sense for Cuckoo to be the source of power behind Setto- heck, it could be that her Ompahlus Stone shards are used to make the charms the Hototogisu uses in modern times. The Pangaean's ability to resonate with other realities and Cuckoo's power over thievery may make her into a &quot;anti Dark Mother&quot; of some sort- connecting the supernatural world through fake Kinship. Heck, she may very well <i>be the Dark Mother</i>, but that has implications which are much greater upon the whole CofD setting. As a false Dark Mother, Cuckoo would try to worm into the nests of other monsters and take from them whatever she wants. Originally, she may very well have been a low god in the divine hierarchy of Pangaea, laying in hideout centuries after the Sundering- and then came Inoue, and everything changed.<br /> <br /> Inoue could be the closest thing that Cuckoo may have for a physical avatar- a person which resonates strangely with her themes and desires, forming a channel to control the whole supernatural community. Either by chance or by design, Inoue may have stumbled upon Cuckoo, and the fateful meeting have changed the world. Maybe Inoue had another name during that time- before he stole the name and immortality of the original Inoue. It could even be that Inoue lives in name only, becoming a parasitic identity which manifests itself every time that an opportunity is brought to his attention. Inoue Akio may be the Mantle of the Cuckoo, the Hototogisu Incarnated- or just a plain old mortal who managed to steal from the Cuckoo, earning her favor and gifts. Setto may in essence be the result of Cuckoo stealing the God Machine's own Infrastructure- or even the ability to produce them, and then subverting them. She stole the mechanisms that the God Machine use to grant boons and demons use for Pacts, she stole the Kinship of the Dark Mother, she stole the relation of the Strix to death and the Kindred... She stole it all, and without Wolf around to stop her and with Inoue's ingenuity to utilize it, she has become unstoppable... with the exception that Inoue have probably stole her as well. Cunning humans with their cunning magic.<br /> <br /> That's the key point- Inoue is the Apex. He controls Tokyo's night. As such, he is probably in control over the ancient theoretical Pangaean as well. Here we are talking about someone who have lived for centuries using stolen immortality and which put the whole vampire society under his thumb. If someone is able to trick a God of Lies, it would be this guy. He is the one to control the pseudo-Infrastructure that gives Cuckoo her ability to manifest and craft charms as well as unifying Tokyo's shadows under his control. The Maze trait? It is not Cuckoo- it is 100% Inoue, 100% his own twisting mind which gives only one right way for success, a product of delicate manipulation and plans which all lead towards a single goal. And if he indeed have subverted the mechanisms of the God Machine through Cuckoo, it could be that you can't actually kill the guy- that he is a living Cover, and that his death will be only a setback as the stolen reality manipulation would allow him to respawn as the same Inoue Akio, same merchant, a plain old mortal with confusing ties to the world. And the interest in vampires? again, yet another expression for his control over the darkness- vampires are the product of disparate Curses bringing the dead back to life, after all, which is held by strange sympathy of the Blood. Inoue stealing that sympathy and name from the vampire may very well be the key for his control over the All Night Society, both socially and metaphysically.<br /> <br /> Now, this is the point where we are to ask ourselves about what is the Hototogisu's true goal- but it is pretty obvious, isn't it? The Hototogisu want to take over the world. They want to steal the powers of the monsters to themselves. Not only that, they want to break the boundary between humans and monsters- the supernatural will be part of the natural, meant to help it progress and evolve. Monsters will be like humans, humans will be like monsters. No one will know the different between truth and lies- an eternal Masquerade where identity is simply the lie you want to be true. And all will be under the strict hierarchy of the same Inoue Akio, the same merchant, the same plain old mortal. Cross the boundary between humanity and monstrosity and true power can be achieved. We are not driving the monsters into the light- we join them in the darkness, snuffing out the light. The monsters by themselves will not know who is a monster and who is a hunter, and when the lines will be blurred it is the time to take over the darkness from within. As they say, if you can't them- be them. Fake it until you make it. And when the time is right, cut down their throat and watch them spitting blood as you take their place in the darkness. Steal from them all you can and throw the leftovers. By the time they'll notice something is wrong, it is too late- the Cuckoo is already here. The Cuckoo is already you.<br /> <br /> We are all Inoue Akio. We just don't know it yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well! Finally- the last conspiracy in the list. That was quite a ride- the last theory is indeed the wildest of them all, I think. If I'll be in the mood I'll start moving through certain compacts next (not all of them, only those I would view as &quot;conspiracy worthy&quot;), but I make no promises. Hope you enjoyed reading those crazy theories, and I hope to make some more in the future :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 02-25-2022, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}